meta {
  name: Parse [Refused]
  type: grpc
  seq: 10
}

grpc {
  url: {{server}}
  method: /recordsimilarity.v1.Quantities/Parse
  body: grpc
  protoPath: ../crates/similarity-proto/proto/recordsimilarity/v1/similarity.proto
  auth: none
  methodType: unary
}

body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "texts": [
        "",
        "Blueberry Gummies 100mg",
        "3.5",
        "3,5 g",
        "1.2.3 g",
        "-1 g",
        "22-18 %",
        "500 mg - 1 g",
        "10 x 10 mg",
        "<1 %",
        "3.5 g (1/8 oz)",
        "half"
      ]
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  A text that is not an amount is an answer with the reason, not an error, and nothing is guessed. In order:
  
  - an empty text: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_EMPTY`
  - `Blueberry Gummies 100mg`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_NO_NUMBER`. Nothing is looked for inside prose.
  - `3.5`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_NO_UNIT`
  - `3,5 g`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_AMBIGUOUS_SEPARATOR`
  - `1.2.3 g`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_BAD_NUMBER`
  - `-1 g`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_NEGATIVE`
  - `22-18 %`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_BACKWARDS_RANGE`
  - `500 mg - 1 g`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_MIXED_UNITS`
  - `10 x 10 mg`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_MULTIPLE`
  - `<1 %`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_QUALIFIED`
  - `3.5 g (1/8 oz)`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_UNREADABLE_UNIT`
  - `half`: `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_AMBIGUOUS_NAME`
  
  More than 1000 texts in one call is `INVALID_ARGUMENT`.
}
